# AmL bird loader — official AOW loading animation

The low-poly hummingbird is the **official AmL logo and loading animation**.
App Builder owns the brand source (`aiapp_builder2/brand/app-builder/`); the
runtime widget and assets live in the **canonical** package:

```
global-assets/packages/aml_ui/
  lib/src/bird_loader.dart       # BirdLoader + BirdRefreshIndicator
  lib/src/settings_about_hero.dart
  assets/bird_loader/*.png
```

Edit `aml_ui` only in `global-assets`. Flutter apps import it with
`path: ../../global-assets/packages/aml_ui` — **no per-repo vendoring**.

Regenerate loader PNGs from App Builder brand:

```powershell
cd C:\Users\ambru\source\repos\aml-systems\aiapp_builder2
python .\scripts\generate-brand-assets.py
```

## Frozen tempo — every AmL app

This is the official **fast** hover. Do **not** slow it for chat, lists,
performance, or “calmer” motion. App Builder Settings is the visual reference.

| | Flutter (`BirdLoader`) | App Builder CSS | `pivots.json` |
|---|---|---|---|
| Wing flap | `flapHalfDuration` **120ms** | `birdWingFlap` **120ms** alternate | `flapPeriodMs` **240** |
| Hover bob | `bobDuration` **350ms** | `birdBob` **350ms** alternate | `bobPeriodMs` **700** |
| Flap angle | `flapRadians` **±12°** | `rotate(±12deg)` | `flapDegrees` **12** |
| Curve | `Curves.easeInOut` | `ease-in-out` | — |

Update all three files together if the user **explicitly** asks to change tempo.
Never change only Flutter or only CSS.

```
❌ 250ms flap / 1000ms bob / ±8°   (slow draft — never ship)
❌ Slowing the bird “so chat stays smooth”
❌ A second, slower loader for chat, Settings, or pull-to-refresh
❌ Per-app durations or a local bird_loader.dart copy
```

## Hard rules — every Flutter app

1. **Use `BirdLoader` from `package:aml_ui/aml_ui.dart`** for indeterminate
   loading — full-screen waits, list skeletons, modal busy states,
   scanner warm-up, etc. A **small inline** spinner inside a control that
   already carries its own label may stay Material. See *Allowed to keep
   Material progress indicators*.
2. **Use `BirdRefreshIndicator`** instead of Material `RefreshIndicator` for
   pull-to-refresh.
3. **Every Settings screen** must open with `SettingsAboutHero` at the top
   (animated bird → product name → version), matching App Builder's layout.
4. **Never add a second copy** of the loader widget or bird PNGs inside an app
   repo. Import from `aml_ui` only.
5. After pivot/timing changes (only if the user asked), update `BirdLoader`
   constants in `aml_ui/lib/src/bird_loader.dart` and the matching App Builder
   web CSS (`apps/web/app/styles.css`) plus `pivots.json`.

## MessageMe exception

MessageMe **keeps** its own loaders for chat identity:

- `AppLoader` (3-dot orbit / bubble spectacular)
- `MessagemeRefreshIndicator`
- `TypingIndicatorBubble` (chat typing dots)

Do **not** replace those. MessageMe still uses `BirdLoader` / `SettingsAboutHero`
for the Settings About hero and any **non-chat** family-branded surfaces.
Those family surfaces use the **same fast tempo** as every other AmL app.

## Allowed to keep Material progress indicators

- **Determinate** progress: `LinearProgressIndicator`, `CircularProgressIndicator(value: …)`
- OneAuth TOTP countdown ring on home cards (`CircularProgressIndicator` with `value`)
- Upload/download/sync percentage bars
- Desktop/Linux fallback inside MessageMe `AppLoader` only
- Small **inline indeterminate** spinners inside a control that already
  carries its own label: a busy button, a chip, a list row trailing slot.
  Keep them small (about 16-20px) with `strokeWidth: 2`. A bird at that size
  is a smudge, and one bird per row turns a list into a flock.

## Forbidden

```
❌ CircularProgressIndicator() for a full-screen, section, or list wait in new code
❌ A bird crammed into a button, chip, or row slot (use a small Material spinner)
❌ RefreshIndicator for pull-to-refresh in new code
❌ Copying bird_loader.dart or bird PNGs into app/lib or app/assets
❌ Settings screen without SettingsAboutHero at the top
❌ Vendoring aml_ui into product repos (use global-assets)
❌ Slowing BirdLoader / CSS / pivots for performance or chat smoothness
```

## New AmL Flutter apps

On day one:

1. Add `aml_ui: path: ../../global-assets/packages/aml_ui` to `app/pubspec.yaml`
2. Settings → `SettingsAboutHero` at top of `ListView`
3. Screen- and section-level loading → `BirdLoader` or `BirdRefreshIndicator`
4. Copy this file to `.cursor/rules/aml-bird-loader.mdc` with `alwaysApply: true`
